---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Decode call data, revert data or a log with an ABI, offline

Usage: rustman evm decode [OPTIONS] --abi <ABI> <HEX>

Arguments:
  <HEX>
          Call data, revert data or log data, as 0x-prefixed hex

Options:
      --abi <ABI>
          The ABI: erc20, erc721, erc1155, or a JSON ABI or Foundry/Hardhat artifact path from the workspace root

      --topic <TOPIC>
          A log topic (repeatable, topic 0 first): decode DATA as a log

      --json
          Print one JSON object instead of text

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
